/**
 * TERRA BELLUM — the offline world.
 *
 * A complete, authoritative implementation of {@link IBackend} that runs the
 * entire game locally: world generation, economy ticks, army movement, capture
 * timers, fortification and production queues, spy drones, transfers, weekly
 * sector rotation, the season clock, rival-guild AI, and the full tactical
 * battle layer including server-equivalent dice and auto-defense.
 *
 * ── Ownership model ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 * `this.live` is the single mutable GameState. Nothing outside this class ever
 * sees it. Every push builds a fresh snapshot: a new root object, new container
 * objects for every collection, freshly cloned player/guild/army/drone records
 * and a deep-cloned `battle`. The render layer therefore never observes a
 * mutation through a reference it already holds.
 *
 * Hex records are re-published inside a *new* `hexes` map but keep their own
 * identity: there are ~500 of them, they are re-read by value every sync by the
 * hex field renderer, and cloning them at 5 Hz would be pure garbage pressure
 * for no observable benefit.
 *
 * ── Clock ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 * Simulated time advances at `SIM.timeScale`× real time so a season is
 * observable in one sitting. While a battle is on the board the scale drops to
 * 1× — the turn timer in `BATTLE.turnMs` is that many real seconds, and the
 * world does not fight a week-long war behind the player's back while they take
 * their turn.
 */
