/**
 * TERRA BELLUM — the server contract.
 *
 * ╔═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╗
 * ║ FIRESTORE SECURITY-RULE INTENT                                            ║
 * ║                                                                           ║
 * ║ The client is a renderer with opinions, never an authority. Concretely:   ║
 * ║                                                                           ║
 * ║  • `worlds/{world}` and `worlds/{world}/hexes/**` — READ for any signed-in ║
 * ║    player, WRITE denied to every client without exception. Ownership,     ║
 * ║    capture timers, fort levels and production queues are Cloud-Function   ║
 * ║    territory. A client that could write a hex could grant itself the map. ║
 * ║                                                                           ║
 * ║  • `worlds/{world}/players/{uid}` — READ for any signed-in player.        ║
 * ║    WRITE limited to the owning uid AND limited to the cosmetic fields     ║
 * ║    (`name`, `hue`). `minerals`, `gas`, `harvested`, `deployed` and        ║
 * ║    `guildId` are function-only: stockpiles are never client-writable.     ║
 * ║                                                                           ║
 * ║  • `armies`, `drones`, `transfers`, `trades`, `treaties`, `parleys`,      ║
 * ║    `objectives`, `marks`, `pings`, `guilds`, `seasons`, `intel` —         ║
 * ║    READ scoped by guild membership where the data is private (intel,      ║
 * ║    officer chat, draft treaties); WRITE denied. Every mutation arrives     ║
 * ║    through the callables below so the server can charge the cost, run the ║
 * ║    timers and write the audit trail.                                      ║
 * ║                                                                           ║
 * ║  • `chat/{id}` — CREATE allowed for the authenticated author when         ║
 * ║    `authorId == request.auth.uid`, `kind == 'text'`, the channel is one   ║
 * ║    the author may post in, and `at == request.time`. No update, no        ║
 * ║    delete. System messages (`kind != 'text'`) are function-only.          ║
 * ║                                                                           ║
 * ║ REALTIME DATABASE                                                         ║
 * ║                                                                           ║
 * ║  • `battles/{world}/{battleId}` — READ for the two participants.          ║
 * ║    WRITE denied. THE DICE ARE ROLLED SERVER-SIDE inside a transaction and ║
 * ║    signed into the battle log (GDD §7.2). A client that could write the   ║
 * ║    battle node could write its own 4-4-4.                                 ║
 * ║                                                                           ║
 * ║  • `presence/{world}/{uid}` — READ for any signed-in player, WRITE for    ║
 * ║    the owning uid only (this is the one authoritative-ish thing a client  ║
 * ║    may touch, and it is mirrored into `Player.online` by a trigger).      ║
 * ║                                                                           ║
 * ║  • `battleQueue/{world}/{uid}` — READ for the owning uid, WRITE denied.   ║
 * ╚═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╝
 *
 * Everything below is a *description of the server*, expressed as types. The
 * client never implements these; it only calls them. Keeping the request and
 * response shapes here means the Cloud Functions package can import this exact
 * file and the contract cannot drift.
 *
 * This module imports nothing from the `firebase` package: it receives an
 * already-bound invoker so the mock path never pays for the SDK.
 */
